  "notes": "A formal term for the deliberate termination of a pregnancy, carrying a legal and clinical tone. In everyday speech {中絶|ちゅうぜつ}, or {人工|じんこう}{妊娠|にんしん}{中絶|ちゅうぜつ}, is far more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {堕胎|だたい}する: to have or perform an abortion\n- {堕胎|だたい}{罪|ざい}: the crime of illegal abortion\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {中絶|ちゅうぜつ}: termination — the ordinary, everyday word\n- {流産|りゅうざん}: miscarriage — spontaneous, not deliberate",
